    "protein_name": "PPE family protein PPE36",
    "ec": [],
    "function": "Heme-binding protein essential for heme utilization (PubMed:28119467). It may be involved in heme translocation across the outer membrane (PubMed:28119467)..; FUNCTION: PPE36 can modulate host inflammatory responses (PubMed:33959974, PubMed:35237255). It can significantly inhibit the M1 polarization of macrophages and reduce the expression of pro-inflammatory cytokines, thereby preventing the occurrence of the host cytokine storm (PubMed:33959974). This inhibitory effect depends on the MAPK/ERK pathway signaling (PubMed:33959974). It can promote the ubiquitination and degradation of the host MyD88 protein by facilitating the interaction of MyD88 with the E3 ligase SMURF1 and then suppress the subsequent NF-kappa-B as well as MAPK pathways, leading to the dampened host inflammatory responses and increased bacterial loads in infected macrophages (PubMed:35237255). In the mouse model, PPE36 significantly reduces the expression of inflammatory cytokines in the immune organs of mice and greatly attenuates the inflammatory damage to the liver, spleen and lungs (PubMed:33959974)..",
